WEBVTT

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.100
That's it for today, class.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.867
Be careful on your way home.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:28.933
Hey, Chie!

00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:30.900
You're going to Poitier today, right?

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.767
For sure! On the way home!

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.467
Yeah! I'll go too!

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:38.400
You won't get any taller by eating cake.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.567
Oh, Mai?

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:44.067
You want to come along?
It's an all-you-can-eat cake buffet.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.533
Definitely!

00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:47.500
Oh, hang on...

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.500
I've got to go to work.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.400
See ya.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.767
Too bad.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:56.733
I guess Tokiha's shift starts now.

00:00:56.733 --> 00:00:59.467
Oh, yeah. You two work at the same place.

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:01.067
With Higurashi!

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:03.667
Will you stop it with that creepy laugh?

00:01:12.867 --> 00:01:18.500
"My-HiME"

00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:22.667
<i>All across the blue sky</i>

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:26.333
<i>our feelings</i>

00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:29.867
<i>are being mounted like gems</i>

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:34.400
<i>If only you were</i>

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>my soul mate</i>

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:44.067
<i>but reality doesn't work that way</i>

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:49.533
<i>In the sparkling wind</i>

00:01:49.533 --> 00:01:56.833
<i>the wings of dreams descend</i>

00:01:56.833 --> 00:02:00.567
<i>Gather the courage to go into the future</i>

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:05.433
<i>with beauty</i>

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.800
<i>The hot heartbeats begin to pulse</i>

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.000
<i>at the same speed</i>

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.900
<i>I felt that day</i>

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:25.967
<i>I like direct gazes</i>

00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:33.700
<i>I want to stare forever</i>

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.433
"Rain -- Tears…"

00:02:42.433 --> 00:02:43.867
"Rain -- Tears…"
It's raining.

00:02:43.867 --> 00:02:45.700
"Rain -- Tears…"

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.367
--Your lunch always looks so yummy.
--Doesn't it?

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.600
My mom and I make
lunch together in the mornings!

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.900
Wow! Lucky you!

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.000
Aren't I?

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:36.433
Um... Miyu?

00:03:36.433 --> 00:03:37.600
You want to come under?

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.033
I can walk you to the chapel.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:42.833
An umbrella... right.
I guess it is raining.

00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:45.000
We're right in the
middle of the rainy season.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.400
A seasonal rain front is moving north.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.533
It's expected to pass
through to the Sea of Japan

00:03:49.533 --> 00:03:51.767
between this evening and tomorrow.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.400
Uh, right.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:58.867
Um, I heard that you're
the daughter of Father Greer.

00:03:58.867 --> 00:04:01.900
Joseph Greer is officially
my adoptive father.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.833
Is that a problem?

00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:04.000
Uh, no...

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.367
Um...

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:07.533
Isn't the chapel that way?

00:04:07.533 --> 00:04:09.833
Take the path to the right.
And go straight.

00:04:09.833 --> 00:04:11.567
Y-Yeah, thought so.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.833
Then turn left after 300 meters.

00:04:13.833 --> 00:04:14.833
Right.

00:04:16.733 --> 00:04:18.633
I was thinking,

00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:20.000
why don't we go to
the beach or something?

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.700
Maybe even take a trip to Okinawa!

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:24.067
What? No way! Really?!

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:28.000
They're working hard so they
can save up for their summer trip.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.033
It's nice to be young.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.633
And since we were hungry,

00:04:35.633 --> 00:04:38.967
we thought we'd come cheer up
our friend who's slaving away at her job.

00:04:38.967 --> 00:04:40.833
You're too kind.

00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:46.400
Hey, Mai. I heard that Takumi
Tokiha is your little brother.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.933
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:47.933 --> 00:04:51.667
Is it true he's rooming with
Akira Okuzaki in the dormitory?

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:53.333
What? I haven't heard that.

00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:54.633
Is he really?

00:04:54.633 --> 00:04:56.333
Yeah, that's pretty much the story.

00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:58.967
I don't think you understand, Mai.

00:04:58.967 --> 00:05:00.733
Think of the implications.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:03.900
The top ranked "pretty boy"
at our school, Akira Okuzaki,

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.433
is rooming with the new
rising star, Takumi Tokiha.

00:05:07.433 --> 00:05:10.867
Picture them sleeping and waking up
in the same room every day.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.667
Just the two of them...

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:15.400
Together morning and night...

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.800
Think of what could happen!

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.867
That's my little brother!

00:05:19.867 --> 00:05:22.833
Don't be dragging him into
your twisted imaginations.

00:05:22.833 --> 00:05:25.467
Oh, right. The big sister.

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:27.333
Anyway, from what I hear,

00:05:27.333 --> 00:05:30.033
I don't think there's
anything to worry about.

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:33.600
Hey, Akira, I ended up making
too much dinner for myself.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.000
You want some?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.500
Don't be such a wus!

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.333
Real men don't cook!

00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:41.333
Are you out of your mind?!

00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:42.600
Well, I just...

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.867
Feet!

00:05:44.867 --> 00:05:47.900
Your feet are over the line!

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:50.033
Uh, sorry.

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:52.000
So what about dinner?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.333
Look, you...!

00:05:54.333 --> 00:05:55.967
Sounds pretty crazy to me.

00:05:55.967 --> 00:05:58.467
It would be nice if they got along.

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:00.867
Akira sure is cute.

00:06:00.867 --> 00:06:03.400
By the way, Mai, do you like karaoke?

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.467
I love it!

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:07.700
We've got a free coupon
that's good until tomorrow.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.833
Well? Tomorrow's a day off.

00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:12.733
A day off, huh...

00:06:12.733 --> 00:06:15.967
Actually, I'm working
first thing in the morning.

00:06:15.967 --> 00:06:19.700
Sorry. I have to pass,
but I'll go next time for sure!

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:23.433
She turned us down again.

00:06:23.433 --> 00:06:25.533
What's she going to do
with all that money she's saving?

00:06:25.533 --> 00:06:28.500
I'm sure Mai's got a reason
for doing what she does.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:29.567
Let's not pry.

00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:30.767
Yeah, but...

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:32.033
Just drop it.

00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:41.600
Hello?

00:06:43.833 --> 00:06:45.533
Mikoto?

00:06:50.833 --> 00:06:52.367
Mikoto!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.433
Hey! What happened to you?!

00:06:58.367 --> 00:07:01.333
I'm starving...

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.033
Why have you been waiting all this time?

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:09.067
I showed you how to buy
meal tickets for the cafeteria.

00:07:09.067 --> 00:07:11.067
Your food's better.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:13.700
Uh, nice try.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.733
But it won't get you any more food.

00:07:35.067 --> 00:07:37.833
Why does she always have to...

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:52.000
Mai?

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.600
"For Mikoto"

00:07:54.467 --> 00:07:55.833
"I'm off to work.

00:07:55.833 --> 00:07:57.867
I'll make you dinner when I get home,

00:07:57.867 --> 00:08:00.100
but you'll have to
manage lunch on your own.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.600
Mai."

00:08:01.933 --> 00:08:04.100
So, how are things going with Akira?

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.833
There's always some kind of trouble.

00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:09.533
But we are slowly starting to get along.

00:08:09.533 --> 00:08:10.433
Right.

00:08:10.433 --> 00:08:11.867
I guess there's nothing to worry about.

00:08:11.867 --> 00:08:12.767
Nope.

00:08:12.767 --> 00:08:14.400
I'm getting used to my classes,

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:17.533
and Kanzaki's been
pretty nice to me at the dorm.

00:08:17.533 --> 00:08:19.467
What about you?

00:08:19.467 --> 00:08:22.733
I'm okay, I guess.

00:08:22.733 --> 00:08:24.067
Actually, I'm having a good time.

00:08:25.967 --> 00:08:27.700
You have your introduction letter?

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:28.467
Yeah.

00:08:28.467 --> 00:08:32.467
And make sure you say hello
to the transplant coordinators.

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:36.400
I know. Hey, Sis, are you sure...

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.967
We already sorted it all out
before we came to this school.

00:08:39.967 --> 00:08:42.000
But still...

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.467
If you bring it up again,

00:08:44.467 --> 00:08:47.567
I'll tell everyone how you
insisted on taking baths with me

00:08:47.567 --> 00:08:48.833
up until just recently.

00:08:48.833 --> 00:08:49.833
Sis!

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.900
I must be imagining things.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.933
Well! I'd better get to work!

00:09:13.933 --> 00:09:15.033
Wait!

00:09:15.033 --> 00:09:17.767
I'm coming!

00:09:17.767 --> 00:09:20.667
Thank you!

00:09:20.667 --> 00:09:22.333
Mr. Sawada.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:41.667
I'm going to send it off to an
American hospital for analysis.

00:09:41.667 --> 00:09:43.500
I appreciate it.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:46.367
Doctor, there's been a
bus accident on the highway.

00:09:46.367 --> 00:09:47.967
Ambulances will be here in five minutes.

00:09:47.967 --> 00:09:50.867
All right, Takumi, I'll talk to you later.

00:09:50.867 --> 00:09:53.600
Okay. Thanks very much.

00:09:54.367 --> 00:09:56.333
Hey, did you hear?

00:09:56.333 --> 00:09:57.900
About Mr. Sawada?

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.400
I saw it on TV.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.633
I heard he was badly injured.

00:10:01.633 --> 00:10:04.033
You take that bus all the time, right?

00:10:04.033 --> 00:10:05.700
Yeah.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.600
I got so worried when
I heard about it on the news.

00:10:08.833 --> 00:10:10.567
Good morning.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.533
Good morning.

00:10:17.533 --> 00:10:20.000
He's been hospitalized
at your dad's, right?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.600
Yeah, I asked Dad about him,
and he said it's not life-threatening.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.567
But it'll take some
time for him to recover.

00:10:25.567 --> 00:10:28.867
Mr. Sawada's getting
on in years, after all.

00:10:28.867 --> 00:10:30.100
That time...

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.100
It can't be.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.733
Mai?

00:10:35.733 --> 00:10:37.833
What's the matter? You look pale.

00:10:37.833 --> 00:10:39.967
The day's just starting. Get it together.

00:10:39.967 --> 00:10:43.067
Uh, really? I feel totally fine!

00:10:43.067 --> 00:10:44.933
Let's go to the café for lunch today!

00:10:44.933 --> 00:10:47.533
Sure. I'll bring Mikoto along, too.

00:10:47.533 --> 00:10:49.433
Take your seats!

00:10:49.433 --> 00:10:52.367
Yes. They're the ones who caused it.

00:10:52.367 --> 00:10:55.533
Our people are already dealing with them.

00:10:55.533 --> 00:10:59.467
I have to say, Mr. Sawada sure was unlucky.

00:10:59.467 --> 00:11:01.567
At least he's been stabilized.

00:11:01.567 --> 00:11:04.833
And it looks like he'll be
moved to a regular hospital.

00:11:04.833 --> 00:11:05.833
What about the Orphan?

00:11:05.833 --> 00:11:07.000
Absolutely no idea.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.400
However...

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.733
...there is evidence of
a battle having taken place.

00:11:11.733 --> 00:11:13.533
With another HiME.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.833
I understand.

00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:19.900
Yoshina will take care of things on this end.

00:11:21.633 --> 00:11:22.967
I'll make some tea.

00:11:22.967 --> 00:11:24.933
You should take a little break.

00:11:24.933 --> 00:11:26.867
Thank you, Fumi.

00:11:32.467 --> 00:11:35.600
It may be their destiny as HiME,

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:38.467
but we've forced a very
difficult mission on them.

00:11:39.933 --> 00:11:43.567
How cruel...

00:11:43.567 --> 00:11:46.467
Hello! Anybody in there?!

00:11:46.467 --> 00:11:47.633
What?

00:11:47.633 --> 00:11:50.633
That.

00:11:50.633 --> 00:11:51.967
Come on, Mikoto.

00:11:51.967 --> 00:11:53.767
Don't drop your food.

00:11:53.767 --> 00:11:56.733
I'll have it!

00:11:56.733 --> 00:11:58.500
Mai?

00:11:58.500 --> 00:11:59.933
We can go and see him.

00:11:59.933 --> 00:12:02.767
Good. We'll visit on behalf of the girls...

00:12:02.767 --> 00:12:05.500
And I, along with Tate,
maybe, can represent the boys.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.100
I just saw him. Over there!

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:10.567
And we'll ask the
others if they want in...

00:12:10.567 --> 00:12:14.500
Changing the subject here,
but does Tokiha have a younger brother?

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.933
She sure does. His name is Takumi.

00:12:16.933 --> 00:12:18.933
Right. That's what I thought.

00:12:18.933 --> 00:12:20.367
I get it.

00:12:20.367 --> 00:12:22.600
That's why she works so hard.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:23.867
What do you mean?

00:12:23.867 --> 00:12:26.800
It's like this...

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.500
Takumi is?!

00:12:39.633 --> 00:12:40.500
Flowers...

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:41.433
Fruit...

00:12:41.433 --> 00:12:42.533
And cold tea.

00:12:42.533 --> 00:12:43.467
That's it.

00:12:43.467 --> 00:12:45.467
What about the bus fare?

00:12:47.933 --> 00:12:49.667
We've got everything covered.

00:12:49.667 --> 00:12:51.867
Hey, you guys free tonight?

00:12:51.867 --> 00:12:54.667
I really feel like getting out
and singing karaoke!

00:12:54.667 --> 00:12:55.467
What do you say?

00:12:55.467 --> 00:12:59.567
Let's have fun! I'll make up
for all the times I didn't go!

00:12:59.567 --> 00:13:00.667
Sorry!

00:13:00.667 --> 00:13:03.433
I'm kind of busy today, too.

00:13:03.433 --> 00:13:05.100
Uh, right...

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:07.967
We're really sorry, Mai.

00:13:07.967 --> 00:13:10.833
No. It's my fault for springing
it on you guys like this.

00:13:10.833 --> 00:13:11.967
Don't worry about it.

00:13:11.967 --> 00:13:12.967
Okay?

00:13:16.433 --> 00:13:20.433
Just my luck. Everyone's busy
with their school clubs today.

00:13:23.433 --> 00:13:24.600
Come on! Let's hurry
before they're all gone!

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:28.500
Yeah, before they're gone!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:30.833
Taking a day off work is great and all,

00:13:30.833 --> 00:13:35.633
but there's nothing for me to do.

00:13:35.633 --> 00:13:37.567
Might as well go home.

00:14:09.667 --> 00:14:12.467
I've already decided that
I'd have nothing to do with it.

00:14:21.933 --> 00:14:24.567
Why?

00:14:24.567 --> 00:14:26.100
Aww!

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:35.667
Please follow that bus!

00:14:35.667 --> 00:14:36.400
Bus?

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:36.900
Yes!

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:39.533
Um, as far as this will take me!

00:14:49.367 --> 00:14:51.533
You can let me out here!

00:14:56.467 --> 00:14:57.933
Oh, Miss! Your change!

00:14:57.933 --> 00:14:59.367
And your bag!

00:15:26.033 --> 00:15:27.433
A monster...

00:15:27.433 --> 00:15:29.433
What was that thing?!

00:15:34.633 --> 00:15:35.533
Kuga?

00:15:35.533 --> 00:15:37.533
Damn! It got away!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.033
They sure got here fast.

00:15:43.033 --> 00:15:44.667
Come on!

00:15:44.667 --> 00:15:45.767
Hurry!

00:15:55.733 --> 00:15:57.833
Who are those people?

00:15:57.833 --> 00:16:01.433
They're from an
organization called "District 1."

00:16:01.433 --> 00:16:03.533
They're gathering HiME at the school.

00:16:03.533 --> 00:16:07.333
And check it out,
those ambulances aren't real.

00:16:07.333 --> 00:16:10.033
They're sent to hospitals and
clinics that are affiliated with them.

00:16:10.033 --> 00:16:13.600
And witnesses are "processed"
so they have no memory of what happened.

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.900
You can't be serious.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:23.600
I don't know what you
think about your powers,

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:25.433
but this is our reality.

00:16:25.433 --> 00:16:27.900
The reality that we HiME have to deal with.

00:16:32.833 --> 00:16:34.833
Yukimi No. 4's already transporting?

00:16:34.833 --> 00:16:36.933
I didn't hear about that.

00:16:36.933 --> 00:16:38.700
Over there.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:41.567
Hey! Are you hurt?!

00:16:41.567 --> 00:16:44.333
Are you all right?

00:16:44.333 --> 00:16:45.600
This girl needs treatment!

00:17:05.567 --> 00:17:08.333
Hey, how come you're here?

00:17:08.333 --> 00:17:09.867
What? You guys!

00:17:09.867 --> 00:17:11.600
Mai...

00:17:12.733 --> 00:17:13.467
"Internal/External Medicine"
"Rehabilitation"

00:17:13.467 --> 00:17:15.000
What's the matter with you guys?

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:18.367
Didn't you tell Mai that we were
coming to visit Mr. Sawada?

00:17:18.367 --> 00:17:21.367
Weren't we supposed to take up
a collection from everyone in class?

00:17:21.367 --> 00:17:23.367
Were you trying to leave her out?

00:17:23.367 --> 00:17:25.467
Give me a break.
That's an awfully childish thing to do.

00:17:25.467 --> 00:17:26.633
That's not it!

00:17:26.633 --> 00:17:28.467
Then tell me how it is!

00:17:28.467 --> 00:17:30.500
It's just that, well... well...

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.467
It's like this...

00:17:32.467 --> 00:17:36.500
We heard all about Takumi.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:40.033
And that it's really serious.

00:17:40.033 --> 00:17:41.933
How did you hear?

00:17:42.967 --> 00:17:44.500
Huh?!

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:47.567
I just happened to
overhear my dad talking...

00:17:47.567 --> 00:17:48.500
Sorry.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:52.100
We wanted to talk to you,
but it's not exactly easy to bring up.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:58.033
You only just transferred here,
so we didn't want to butt in.

00:18:02.933 --> 00:18:06.800
Oh, come on!
I should be the one to apologize!

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:09.767
I made you guys get
all worried about me.

00:18:09.767 --> 00:18:11.400
You forgive us?

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.833
Of course!

00:18:12.833 --> 00:18:16.467
I mean, there's nothing
for me to forgive!

00:18:16.467 --> 00:18:18.667
Is there?

00:18:18.667 --> 00:18:20.600
But you sure are dedicated.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:22.000
I really admire you.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:24.733
It's no big deal.

00:18:24.733 --> 00:18:28.367
Let me know if you want to
see my notes or study together.

00:18:28.367 --> 00:18:29.500
Thanks!

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.900
Good luck, Mai!

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:34.400
We'll be rooting for you all the way!

00:18:35.667 --> 00:18:36.767
See you.

00:18:36.767 --> 00:18:38.333
See you tomorrow.

00:18:50.933 --> 00:18:53.967
Oh, Mai.

00:18:53.967 --> 00:18:57.933
If you're looking for Takumi,
your father came to pick him up.

00:18:57.933 --> 00:19:01.333
You're such a dedicated girl,
always trying so hard.

00:19:01.333 --> 00:19:03.400
I'll be rooting for you.

00:19:08.433 --> 00:19:11.333
Hey. You still here?

00:19:11.333 --> 00:19:12.700
How come you are?

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:13.833
Just a visit.

00:19:13.833 --> 00:19:16.800
Wanted to say hello to a
doctor who treated me before.

00:19:20.567 --> 00:19:22.400
You don't have an umbrella?

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.500
Don't expect to get under mine.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.900
Whatever.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:28.600
I would've refused even if you offered.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.333
Don't need an umbrella.

00:19:36.733 --> 00:19:39.600
Hey...

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:41.600
H-Hey, hang on!

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:42.967
Hey!

00:19:46.333 --> 00:19:48.000
I said wait!

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:53.533
I was only joking!

00:19:53.533 --> 00:19:57.000
It's just an umbrella...

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.733
Here.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:22.767
Have this.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:26.500
Hot's better.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.967
Huh? Don't be so demanding.

00:20:28.967 --> 00:20:31.633
You know what month it is?

00:20:31.633 --> 00:20:33.900
Just kidding.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.900
I just felt like being spoiled, that's all.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:37.633
Oh, man...

00:20:39.967 --> 00:20:42.633
I'm sorry for all this.

00:20:42.633 --> 00:20:46.033
I just couldn't keep it all inside.

00:20:46.033 --> 00:20:48.600
Does that ever happen to you?

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.533
Never.

00:20:51.533 --> 00:20:53.400
I see.

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:55.067
I suppose.

00:20:57.067 --> 00:20:59.600
You don't say things like that, do you?

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:00.500
Like what?

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:03.800
Like, "I'm rooting for you."

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:05.933
To say something like that...

00:21:05.933 --> 00:21:10.367
...is irresponsible, and not fair
to the one you're saying it to.

00:21:10.367 --> 00:21:14.667
Besides, Mai, I already
know you're doing your best.

00:21:17.633 --> 00:21:20.567
I mean, you know...

00:21:20.567 --> 00:21:24.400
At the very least you
deserve a can of coffee.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:27.533
And a cold can of coffee it is.

00:21:27.533 --> 00:21:30.833
That just means I'm a cool guy.

00:21:33.067 --> 00:21:34.933
What are you talking about?

00:21:34.933 --> 00:21:35.967
Cool?

00:21:35.967 --> 00:21:37.067
Got a problem with that?

00:21:37.067 --> 00:21:38.567
Not really.

00:21:38.567 --> 00:21:40.800
So you think you're cool, huh?

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.100
Look, you...

00:21:44.767 --> 00:21:47.000
Come on, just cut it out.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.400
Hey, Big Brother!

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:49.467
What?!

00:21:49.467 --> 00:21:51.933
Hey, you! Hold it!

00:21:51.933 --> 00:21:53.633
Good morning, Tate!

00:21:55.033 --> 00:21:57.567
Thanks for yesterday.

00:21:57.567 --> 00:21:58.967
Ow! Ow!

00:21:58.967 --> 00:22:01.400
It's hot!

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:03.500
Unlike someone I know,

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:06.400
I don't go out of
my way to try and be cool.

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:10.733
She's such a dork...

00:22:10.733 --> 00:22:13.033
Mai!

00:22:13.033 --> 00:22:16.500
Glad you're back to normal, Mai!

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:18.500
Of course I am!

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:20.733
Come on. Let's go, Mikoto!

00:22:26.733 --> 00:22:32.467
<i>I couldn't tell you not to lose your way</i>

00:22:32.467 --> 00:22:38.000
<i>There are thoughts that'll never reach you</i>

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:43.400
<i>A smile that is too Ionely quivers</i>

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:48.600
<i>I puzzle over my wounds LONELY GOOD-BYE</i>

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:55.333
<i>Even my passion hurts</i>

00:22:55.333 --> 00:23:00.367
<i>as I chase after an eternal fragment</i>

00:23:00.367 --> 00:23:06.933
<i>You were the sky, you were the dream</i>

00:23:06.933 --> 00:23:10.800
<i>The days that burn and melt</i>

00:23:12.567 --> 00:23:18.633
<i>Make them unforgettable memories</i>

00:23:18.633 --> 00:23:23.900
<i>Wear them proudly on your chest</i>

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:25.767
<i>SEARCH FOR MY LIFE</i>

00:23:25.767 --> 00:23:30.033
<i>We will be able to meet again</i>

00:23:30.033 --> 00:23:35.400
<i>I loved those transparent eyes</i>

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:40.433
<i>Now we have our own paths</i>

00:23:40.433 --> 00:23:43.633
<i>carrying on RESTARTING</i>

00:23:56.333 --> 00:23:56.800
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"

00:23:56.800 --> 00:23:58.767
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
The rainy season. Endless rain...

00:23:58.767 --> 00:24:00.400
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
The rain of tears...

00:24:00.400 --> 00:24:01.500
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
I hate rain...

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:01.867
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
Mai?

00:24:01.867 --> 00:24:03.600
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
I hate it when it rains.

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:05.033
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
Come on, Mai! Get a grip!

00:24:05.033 --> 00:24:06.733
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
It's like tears falling from the sky.

00:24:06.733 --> 00:24:09.400
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
Maybe her brain is waterlogged.

00:24:09.400 --> 00:24:11.456
"The Passionate Age of 17 (^^;)"
I definitely don't like rain.
